<title>GREECE: Greece cuts T-bills rates by 10bps effective Mon.</title>
<headline>Greece cuts T-bills rates by 10bps effective Mon.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece will slash three-, six- and 12-month T-bill rates by a tenth of a point to 8.50 percent, 8.80 percent, 9.60 percent respectively from Monday, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>The treasury will issue 12-month T-bills on June 2 via a</p>
<p>public subscription, it added.</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
